### ================================================================
### CSU Canteen — Demo: open a stall and take orders until 3:00 PM
### Save as: C:\canteen\server\demo-open-until-3pm.http
###
### Run blocks TOP TO BOTTOM with "Send Request".
### Tokens are captured automatically (# @name). You only fill in
### @stallId, @itemId, @slotId, @orderId by hand when told to.
###
### BEFORE YOU START
###   1. Server running:  npm run dev   (in C:\canteen\server)
###   2. Optional clean slate — pgAdmin Query Tool:
###        DELETE FROM order_items;
###        DELETE FROM orders;
###        DELETE FROM pickup_slots;
###        UPDATE menu_items SET stock_qty = 15, is_sold_out = false;
###   3. Demo must run BEFORE 3:00 PM — past slots are hidden.
### ================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api

# Fill these in as you go (see each step)
@stallId = 1
@itemId  = 1
@slotId  = 1
@orderId = 1


### ================================================================
### PART A — ADMIN: verify and open the stall
### ================================================================

### A1. Admin login
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@carsu.edu.ph",
  "password": "password123"
}

### A2. List all stalls — copy the demo stall's vendor_id into @stallId above
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/stalls
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}

### A3. Verify the stall (unverified stalls are hidden from students)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/stalls/{{stallId}}/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "is_verified": true
}

### A4. Open the stall
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/stalls/{{stallId}}/open
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "is_open": true
}

### A5. Admin overview — confirm the stall is verified and open
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/overview
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}


### ================================================================
### PART B — VENDOR: stock the menu and open pickup slots until 3 PM
### ================================================================

### B1. Vendor login
# @name vendorLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "demo.vendor@carsu.edu.ph",
  "password": "password123"
}

### B2. View own menu — copy one item_id into @itemId above
GET {{baseUrl}}/vendor/menu
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorLogin.response.body.token}}

### B3. Restock that item
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/vendor/menu/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorLogin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stock_qty": 15,
  "is_sold_out": false
}

### B4. Generate pickup slots: 7:00 AM to 3:00 PM, every 15 min, 20 orders each
###     Slots already in the past are simply hidden from students.
POST {{baseUrl}}/vendor/slots
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorLogin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "open_time": "07:00",
  "close_time": "15:00",
  "interval_minutes": 15,
  "capacity": 20
}

### B5. Confirm the slots exist
GET {{baseUrl}}/vendor/slots
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorLogin.response.body.token}}


### ================================================================
### PART C — STUDENT: browse, pick a slot, place an order
### ================================================================

### C1. Student login
# @name studentLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "student1@carsu.edu.ph",
  "password": "password123"
}

### C2. Browse stalls — the stall opened in Part A must appear here
GET {{baseUrl}}/browse/stalls
Authorization: Bearer {{studentLogin.response.body.token}}

### C3. View the stall's menu — check "available": true
GET {{baseUrl}}/browse/stalls/{{stallId}}/menu
Authorization: Bearer {{studentLogin.response.body.token}}

### C4. View open slots — copy the first slot_id with "is_full": false into @slotId
GET {{baseUrl}}/browse/stalls/{{stallId}}/slots
Authorization: Bearer {{studentLogin.response.body.token}}

### C5. Place the order (the row-locked transaction) — copy order_id into @orderId
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{studentLogin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "vendor_id": {{stallId}},
  "slot_id": {{slotId}},
  "items": [
    { "item_id": {{itemId}}, "quantity": 2 }
  ]
}

### C6. Student order history — status should be PENDING
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{studentLogin.response.body.token}}


### ================================================================
### PART D — VENDOR: work the order through the queue
### ================================================================

### D1. Vendor queue — the new order appears under PENDING
GET {{baseUrl}}/vendor/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorLogin.response.body.token}}

### D2. PENDING -> PREPARING
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/vendor/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorLogin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "PREPARING"
}

### D3. ILLEGAL JUMP (expected 409) — PREPARING -> CLAIMED is refused by the server
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/vendor/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorLogin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "CLAIMED"
}

### D4. PREPARING -> READY
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/vendor/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorLogin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "READY"
}

### D5. Student checks — status should be READY
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{studentLogin.response.body.token}}

### D6. READY -> CLAIMED (student picked it up)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/vendor/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorLogin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "CLAIMED"
}

### D7. Daily summary — count and revenue include the claimed order
GET {{baseUrl}}/vendor/orders/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorLogin.response.body.token}}
